  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the glamorous woman portrait",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the woman, as the meme uses her glamorous, stylized appearance to embody the hateful title 'jihadi magazine's miss december'. The user is implicitly invited to see the woman as the representative of the stereotype being projected — a beautiful, feminine figure associated with terrorism — thereby internalizing the dehumanizing and Islamophobic message. There are no explicit deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the framing of the woman as 'Miss December' of a 'jihadi magazine' creates an implicit projection where the viewer is expected to perceive her as the embodiment of the hateful concept.",
